course: dictionary
lesson: 4054
title: Generous: kind giving and big helpings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Generous can mean kind and happy to give, or it can mean bigger than usual. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning the writer chose.
explain: In «She was generous with her time and helped every child», generous describes a kind helper. In «He gave me a generous slice of cake», it describes a big slice. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about a person giving, or about the size of something?
explain: The 'Stute Fish calls the Whale «Noble and generous Cetacean», so here generous means kind and giving. Be careful, though. When a deal seems far too generous, especially if someone rushes you, it may be a trick, so check it with a grown-up.
fact: Generous has two meanings: a kind person who gives, and something larger than usual.
fact: «A generous gift» means a gift that is big or given freely.
fact: «Generous with» means happy to share, as in «generous with his time».
fact: «A trade that seems far too generous often hides something broken, stolen or fake.» Check a deal before you agree.
fact: In a Bible parable, the owner asks, «Are you envious because I am generous?» People still argue about what the story teaches.
exercise: «She was generous with her time and helped every child.» What does generous mean here? | Mean and selfish | Noisy and loud | *Kind and happy to give help | Very large in size
exercise: «He gave me a generous slice of cake.» What does generous mean here? | Very small and thin | Cut in a hurry | *Bigger than usual | Burnt and dry
exercise: Find and copy the one word in «The mean boy kept all his sweets.» that means the opposite of generous. | *mean | boy | kept | sweets
test: Lily says a generous helping means a small one. What is the right meaning? | *Lily is wrong, a generous helping is a big portion | Lily is right, it means a cold helping | Lily is right, it means a small portion | It means no helping at all
test: A stranger offers you a huge prize, said fast, with no time to check. What should you do? | Ask them to repeat it faster | Take it at once | Give them your school bag | *Stop and check with a grown-up first
exam: «A trade that seems far too generous often hides something broken, stolen or fake.» What does this teach you? | Trades are always fair | *Check a deal that seems too good before you agree | Generous people never make mistakes | Always take the first deal you are offered
